      "start_seconds": 6.35,
      "end_seconds": 10.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "of course, leave it there how can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.02,
      "end_seconds": 19.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "I wanted to get wheezing looked at"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.53,
      "end_seconds": 27.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.67,
      "end_seconds": 31.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "it's been ten days now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.92,
      "end_seconds": 37.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.87,
      "text": "yes, carry on. Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.85,
      "end_seconds": 53.74,
      "duration_seconds": 14.89,
      "text": "The inhaler helps a bit. Maybe a three out of ten on a bad day. It happens on and off. It's worse with cold air and dust. I've also had a night-time cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.67,
      "end_seconds": 60.15,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "Have you had wheezing before or is this the the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.85,
      "end_seconds": 67.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.44,
      "text": "I had a similar thing last year. It It went away"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 68.36,
      "end_seconds": 78.02,
      "duration_seconds": 9.66,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Respiratory rate 25, pulse is 99 beats a a minute, saturation 92 percent. BP is 133 over 74."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.9,
      "end_seconds": 80.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "good, thank you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.38,
      "end_seconds": 85.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "right, let's have a proper look at you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.35,
      "end_seconds": 88.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.01,
      "text": "sure thing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.68,
      "end_seconds": 90.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.83,
      "end_seconds": 110.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "you're speaking in full sentences, which is reassuring"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.22,
      "end_seconds": 113.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "look straight ahead"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.26,
      "end_seconds": 127.44,
      "duration_seconds": 6.18,
      "text": "I can hear a widespread wheeze on both sides when you breathe out"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.2,
      "end_seconds": 134.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "okay, that's enough for me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.83,
      "end_seconds": 148.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Any leg swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.85,
      "end_seconds": 155.39,
      "duration_seconds": 6.54,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, not that I've noticed, no leg swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.22,
      "end_seconds": 159.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Any fever or runny nose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.3,
      "end_seconds": 164.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "no fever or runny nose, none of it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.69,
      "end_seconds": 168.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "And And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.84,
      "end_seconds": 171.78,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "No rashes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.59,
      "end_seconds": 186.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.64,
      "end_seconds": 190.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "No, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.66,
      "end_seconds": 195.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.97,
      "end_seconds": 206.52,
      "duration_seconds": 10.55,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother. I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day. I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.39,
      "end_seconds": 210.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "so, do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.05,
      "end_seconds": 224.22,
      "duration_seconds": 8.17,
      "text": "Asthma, for about ten years. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.39,
      "end_seconds": 226.09,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Ah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.9,
      "end_seconds": 245.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Any regular medication at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 249.42,
      "end_seconds": 252.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "no I don't take any tablets"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.27,
      "end_seconds": 257.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.03,
      "end_seconds": 261.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "yes naproxen i get a rash"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.07,
      "end_seconds": 270.75,
      "duration_seconds": 7.68,
      "text": "Right here's what I'm thinking. I'd lean towards an asthma flare-up. I'd also keep an allergic reaction in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 272.19,
      "end_seconds": 273.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.5,
      "end_seconds": 291.76,
      "duration_seconds": 17.26,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like an asthma flare-up, but I'd like to confirm. Stop me if I've got anything wrong. You've had wheezing for ten days, and no runny nose or leg swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.6,
      "end_seconds": 295.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "that's it, yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.38,
      "end_seconds": 325.06,
      "duration_seconds": 28.68,
      "text": "I'm going to order breathing tests for asthma i'm going to order a chest X-ray for wheeze i'm prescribing Seretide inhaler 250 micrograms two puffs twice a day long term it's for asthma control let me watch you use the inhaler a lot of people don't get the full dose make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids two to three litres a day if you can and get proper rest"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.93,
      "end_seconds": 338.12,
      "duration_seconds": 12.19,
      "text": "please don't wait if the inhaler isn't helping or you can't speak in full sentences that's when to be seen urgently does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 341.82,
      "end_seconds": 344.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "thank you, that's helpful"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 345.94,
      "end_seconds": 347.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ]
